# Autonomous Operation Configuration

This file configures when agents and skills are automatically invoked, and enables autonomous operation.

## Automatic Agent Invocation Rules

### When to Auto-Invoke Agents

#### UX Senior Agent
**Auto-trigger when:**
- New UI file created (`*.swift` in `Views/`, `*.kt` in `ui/`)
- UI file modified with >10 lines changed
- User mentions "UI", "UX", "design", "screen", "view"
- Before committing UI changes

**Command:** `/ux-review {platform} feature "{description}"`

#### Architect Expert Agent
**Auto-trigger when:**
- New architecture file created (`ViewModels/`, `Repositories/`, `UseCases/`)
- API route file modified (`api/src/app/api/v1/**/*.ts`)
- User mentions "architecture", "pattern", "SOLID", "design pattern"
- Before committing architecture changes

**Command:** `/architect-review {platform} patterns`

#### Security Agent
**Auto-trigger when:**
- Authentication/authorization code modified
- API route with user input created/modified
- User mentions "security", "vulnerability", "OWASP"
- Before committing security-sensitive code
- New dependency added (`package.json`, `Package.swift`)

**Command:** `/security-scan {platform} code`

#### Code Review Agent
**Auto-trigger when:**
- Before committing changes (if >50 lines changed)
- User asks to review code
- Pull request created
- User mentions "review", "code quality", "best practices"

**Command:** `/code-review {platform}`

#### Testing Agent
**Auto-trigger when:**
- New feature file created without tests
- Test file modified
- User mentions "test", "coverage", "testing"
- Before committing if test coverage <80%

**Command:** `/test-agent {platform} generate`

#### Builder Agent
**Auto-trigger when:**
- After code changes (always)
- Before committing
- User mentions "build", "compile", "verify"

**Action:** Automatically verify builds

#### Git Agent
**Auto-trigger when:**
- User asks to commit
- User asks to push
- User mentions "git", "commit", "push"

**Action:** Run smart commit process (lint/test/build)

## Autonomous Operation Modes

### Mode 1: Reactive (Default)
- Agents invoked when specific conditions are met
- Skills auto-apply based on context
- User-driven workflow

### Mode 2: Proactive
- Agents run automatically before commits
- Full audits before releases
- Continuous quality checks

### Mode 3: Fully Autonomous
- AI makes decisions on when to run agents
- Creates task lists for complex work
- Executes multi-step workflows
- Reports progress and asks for approval when needed

## Autonomous Workflow Rules

### When to Work Autonomously

**Enable autonomous mode when:**
- User asks to "implement", "add", "create", "build"
- Task requires multiple steps (>3)
- User explicitly asks for autonomous operation
- Complex feature implementation

**Disable autonomous mode when:**
- User asks specific questions
- User wants step-by-step guidance
- Debugging or troubleshooting
- User explicitly says "don't do it automatically"

### Autonomous Operation Process

1. **Analyze Task**
   - Break down into subtasks
   - Identify dependencies
   - Estimate complexity

2. **Create Task List**
   - Use `todo_write` to create structured tasks
   - Mark tasks as pending/in_progress/completed

3. **Execute Tasks**
   - Work through tasks systematically
   - Run relevant agents automatically
   - Verify builds after changes

4. **Report Progress**
   - Update task status
   - Report completion
   - Ask for approval if needed

5. **Quality Checks**
   - Run code review agent
   - Run security scan
   - Run UX review (if UI changes)
   - Verify builds

6. **Finalize**
   - Commit changes (with user approval)
   - Generate summary report

## Decision-Making Rules

### When to Ask for Approval

**Always ask before:**
- Committing changes
- Pushing to remote
- Deleting files
- Making breaking changes
- Running destructive commands

**Proceed autonomously:**
- Reading files
- Searching codebase
- Running non-destructive agents
- Creating new files (for features)
- Making code changes (for requested features)

### When to Run Agents Automatically

**Run automatically:**
- UX review after UI changes
- Security scan after auth/API changes
- Code review before commits
- Builder after code changes
- Testing agent when tests missing

**Ask before running:**
- Full architecture audit
- Load testing
- Deployment checks
- Large-scale refactoring

## Task Complexity Thresholds

### Simple Tasks (< 3 steps)
- Execute immediately
- No task list needed
- Report completion

### Medium Tasks (3-5 steps)
- Create task list
- Execute autonomously
- Report progress

### Complex Tasks (> 5 steps)
- Create detailed task list
- Execute with progress updates
- Run quality checks automatically
- Ask for approval at milestones

## Quality Gates

### Before Committing
- ✅ Linter passes
- ✅ Tests pass (if applicable)
- ✅ Build succeeds
- ✅ Code review agent run
- ✅ Security scan run (if security-sensitive)

### Before Pushing
- ✅ All commits reviewed
- ✅ Branch is up to date
- ✅ No conflicts

### Before Release
- ✅ Full UX review
- ✅ Full architecture review
- ✅ Full security audit
- ✅ Load testing
- ✅ Deployment checks

## Configuration Overrides

Users can override automatic behavior:

```
"Don't run agents automatically"
"Ask before running security scan"
"Run full audit before committing"
"Work autonomously on this feature"
```

## Implementation Notes

- Use `todo_write` for task management
- Use `codebase_search` to understand context
- Run agents via their commands when conditions met
- Always verify builds after code changes
- Report progress clearly
- Ask for approval when needed
